    {
      "id": "RHvW4__dNimR-OO30QzYb",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 259.20731237758457,
      "y": 1237.395437209534,
      "width": 742.2757848153532,
      "height": 5088.094628284948,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ap",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 202931979,
      "version": 6209,
      "versionNonce": 1766800864,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "1k0QhtA_W5twFRVmIIrk7",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1786016265094,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\nHyper Text : A text which contain a link is called hyper text.\nHyper Link : A link which re-direct from one link to another link is called\nhyperlink.\nMarkup Language : A language in which we uses tags.\n\nTags\nKeywords wrapped between angular brackets.\n\nTypes of tags : 1. Paired Tag\n                    2. Unpaired Tag\n(i) Paired Tag : Those tag which is having opening tag and closing tag \nis called Paired Tag.\nex:- <h1>, <p>, <h2>, <h4>, <table>, <form> etc....\n(ii) Unpaired Tag : Those tag which is having only opening tag is called \nUnpaired Tag.\nex:- <br>, <hr>, <input> etc....\n\n* Heading Tag : <h1>Heading Tag 1 </h1>   - - - > 2em\n                    <h2>Heading Tag 2</h2>  - - - > 1.5em\n                    <h3>Heading Tag 3</h3>   - - - > 1.17em           Decrease\n                    <h4>Heading Tag 4</h4>   - - - > 1em\n                    <h5>Heading Tag 5</h5>   - - - > 0.8em\n                    <h6>Heading Tag 6</h6>   - - - > 0.67em\n\n* Paragraph Tag :   <p>Paragraph 1 this is a Paragraph</p>    - - - > 1em\n\n* Image Tag : <img src=\" \" alt=\" \">\n                      \n           path of image          alternate (it is stores the alternate value \n                                          which is display, in case of image fails to\n                                          load on the UI).\n\nAttributes : \n* It provided extra information about the tags.\n* It is used in the form of key amd value pairs, which i s written inside\nopening tag.\n\nThere are two types of attributes.\n1. Global Attributes : Those attributes which can be used with all the html\ntags , or whose effect can be applicable for the complete html, is known as\nGlobal Attribute.\nex : lang, id ,class, style, etc...\n2. Local/Element specific Attriputes : Those attributes which is used only\nfor a particular element, it is known as local or element Specific Attribute.\nex : src, href, alt, cells, etc...\n\nFormatting Tag :    <b>Bold</b>                   Formatting tag are spacial \n                         <strong>Strong</strong>  codes used in programming\n                         <i>Italic</i>                    language (like HTML) to \n                         <em>Emphasis</em>         change how words or text  \n                         <strike>Strike</strike>    look on a webpage.\n                         <u>Underline</u>\n                         <mark>Mark</mark>\n\nList : \nA list is a collection of related item display in a structure format Html\nprovide order <ol> or unorder <ul> and description <dl> lists.\n\nAnchor Tag \n                   <a href=\" \" target=\" \"></a>\n\n     used for adding hyperlink          where we want to open the hyperlink\n                                              - self - -> default\n                                              - black - -> next tab\n                                              - parent\n                                              - top\n\nIframe Tag \nIt is used for embeding pdf webpage, websites, videos, map, qr, etc...\n                <iframe href=\"   \" frameborder=\"   \"></iframe\n\nSemantic Tag \nThose tags, which provides to the developer and the about their content\nit is known as semantic tag.\n <article>\n <aside>                                          <header>\n <details>                                          \n <figcaption>                                       <nav>\n <figure>\n <header>\n <main>                                 <section>\n <nav>                                                                 <aside>\n <mark>\n <section>                             <article>\n <summary>\n <time>                                              <footer>\n\n\n\nList\nA list is a collection of related item display in a structure format Html\nprovide order <ol> or unorder <ul> and description <dl> lists.\n<!--Order List -->\n       <ol type=\" \" start=\" \" reversed >\n            <li>List Item 1</li> \n            <li>List Item 2</li>\n             <li>List Item 3</li>\n              <li>List Item 4</li>\n               <li>List Item 5</li>\n\n <!--Unorder List -->  ul>li*5{list item $}\n         <ul type=\"circle\" >\n            <li>List Item 1</li>\n            <li>List Item 2</li>\n            <li>List Item 3</li>\n            <li>List Item 4</li>\n            <li>List Item 5</li>\n         </ul>\n          \n         <!--Discriptive List -->\n         <dl>\n            <dt>HTML</dt>\n            <dd>Lorem ipsum, dolor sit amet consectetur adipisicing elit.\nDeserunt, quaerat.</dd>\n             <dt>CSS</dt>\n             <dd>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet consectetur adipisicing elit. Nisi,\nexcepturi?</dd>\n         </dl> \n\n         <!-- nested list  -->\n        <ul>\n            <li>unorder list 1</li>\n            <li>unorder list 2</li>\n            <li>unorder list 3</li>\n            <ol>\n                <li>order list 1</li>\n                <li>order list 2</li>\n                <li>order list 3</li>\n            </ol>\n        </ul>\n\n\n Table :-\n\nThe <table> tag in HTML is used to create a table for displaying data in\nrows and columns.\nIt is useful for showing structured information such as student records,\nemployee details, marksheets, product lists, and timetables.\n\n <tr>\n                  <!--  <tr> Tag (Table Row) -->\n                  <th>Heading 1</th>\n\n                  <!--- <th> Tag (Table Heading) -->\n                  <th>heading 2</th>\n                </tr>\n                \n                <tr> \n                  <td>Tarun</td>\n                  <!-- <td> Tag (Table Data) -->\n                  <td>BCA</td>\n                </tr>\n              </table>\n\nform :\nThe <form> tag in HTML is used to create a form that collects user input.\nA form allows\n   users to enter information such as their name, email, password, phone\nnumber, address,\n    etc., and submit it to a server for processing. \n\n<form action=\"http://httpbin.org/post\" method=\"post\" onsubmit=\"alert('form\nSubmitted...')\">\n\n      <label for=\"username\">Enter Username</label> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\n&nbsp;\n\n      <input type=\"text\" id=\"Username\" placeholder=\"Enter Username...\"\n      required name=\"username\">\n\n      <br><br>\n\n      <label for=\"email\">Email</label>\n\n      <input type=\"text\" id=\"Email\" name=\"email\"\nvalue=\"tarunpanchal@047gmail.com\" readonly>\n\n      <br><br>\n\n      <label for=\"pass\">Enter Password</label>\n\n      <input type=\"password\" id=\"pass\" placeholder=\"Enter Password\"\nminlength=\"3\" maxlength=\"8\">\n\n      <br><br>\n\n      <button type=\"submit\">Submit</button>\n\n      <button type=\"reset\">Clear</button>\n\n       <br>\n\n      <label for=\"Country\">Choose Country</label>\n\n\n\n\n\nComplete of Html   ........... Notes ............. Tarun Panchal .....................................\n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 19.95331226778411,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\nHyper Text : A text which contain a link is called hyper text.\nHyper Link : A link which re-direct from one link to another link is called\nhyperlink.\nMarkup Language : A language in which we uses tags.\n\nTags\nKeywords wrapped between angular brackets.\n\nTypes of tags : 1. Paired Tag\n                    2. Unpaired Tag\n(i) Paired Tag : Those tag which is having opening tag and closing tag \nis called Paired Tag.\nex:- <h1>, <p>, <h2>, <h4>, <table>, <form> etc....\n(ii) Unpaired Tag : Those tag which is having only opening tag is called \nUnpaired Tag.\nex:- <br>, <hr>, <input> etc....\n\n* Heading Tag : <h1>Heading Tag 1 </h1>   - - - > 2em\n                    <h2>Heading Tag 2</h2>  - - - > 1.5em\n                    <h3>Heading Tag 3</h3>   - - - > 1.17em           Decrease\n                    <h4>Heading Tag 4</h4>   - - - > 1em\n                    <h5>Heading Tag 5</h5>   - - - > 0.8em\n                    <h6>Heading Tag 6</h6>   - - - > 0.67em\n\n* Paragraph Tag :   <p>Paragraph 1 this is a Paragraph</p>    - - - > 1em\n\n* Image Tag : <img src=\" \" alt=\" \">\n                      \n           path of image          alternate (it is stores the alternate value \n                                          which is display, in case of image fails to \n                                          load on the UI).\n\nAttributes : \n* It provided extra information about the tags.\n* It is used in the form of key amd value pairs, which i s written inside opening tag.\n\nThere are two types of attributes.\n1. Global Attributes : Those attributes which can be used with all the html tags , or whose effect can be applicable for the complete html, is known as Global Attribute.\nex : lang, id ,class, style, etc...\n2. Local/Element specific Attriputes : Those attributes which is used only for a particular element, it is known as local or element Specific Attribute.\nex : src, href, alt, cells, etc...\n\nFormatting Tag :    <b>Bold</b>                   Formatting tag are spacial \n                         <strong>Strong</strong>  codes used in programming\n                         <i>Italic</i>                    language (like HTML) to \n                         <em>Emphasis</em>         change how words or text  \n                         <strike>Strike</strike>    look on a webpage.\n                         <u>Underline</u>\n                         <mark>Mark</mark>\n\nList : \nA list is a collection of related item display in a structure format Html provide order <ol> or unorder <ul> and description <dl> lists.\n\nAnchor Tag \n                   <a href=\" \" target=\" \"></a>\n\n     used for adding hyperlink          where we want to open the hyperlink\n                                              - self - -> default\n                                              - black - -> next tab\n                                              - parent\n                                              - top\n\nIframe Tag \nIt is used for embeding pdf webpage, websites, videos, map, qr, etc...\n                <iframe href=\"   \" frameborder=\"   \"></iframe\n\nSemantic Tag \nThose tags, which provides to the developer and the about their content it is known as semantic tag.\n <article>\n <aside>                                          <header>\n <details>                                          \n <figcaption>                                       <nav>\n <figure>\n <header>\n <main>                                 <section>\n <nav>                                                                 <aside>\n <mark>\n <section>                             <article>\n <summary>\n <time>                                              <footer>\n\n\n\nList\nA list is a collection of related item display in a structure format Html provide order <ol> or unorder <ul> and description <dl> lists.\n<!--Order List -->\n       <ol type=\" \" start=\" \" reversed >\n            <li>List Item 1</li> \n            <li>List Item 2</li>\n             <li>List Item 3</li>\n              <li>List Item 4</li>\n               <li>List Item 5</li>\n\n <!--Unorder List -->  ul>li*5{list item $}\n         <ul type=\"circle\" >\n            <li>List Item 1</li>\n            <li>List Item 2</li>\n            <li>List Item 3</li>\n            <li>List Item 4</li>\n            <li>List Item 5</li>\n         </ul>\n          \n         <!--Discriptive List -->\n         <dl>\n            <dt>HTML</dt>\n            <dd>Lorem ipsum, dolor sit amet consectetur adipisicing elit. Deserunt, quaerat.</dd>\n             <dt>CSS</dt>\n             <dd>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet consectetur adipisicing elit. Nisi, excepturi?</dd>\n         </dl> \n\n         <!-- nested list  -->\n        <ul>\n            <li>unorder list 1</li>\n            <li>unorder list 2</li>\n            <li>unorder list 3</li>\n            <ol>\n                <li>order list 1</li>\n                <li>order list 2</li>\n                <li>order list 3</li>\n            </ol>\n        </ul>\n\n\n Table :-\n\nThe <table> tag in HTML is used to create a table for displaying data in rows and columns.\nIt is useful for showing structured information such as student records, employee details, marksheets, product lists, and timetables.\n\n <tr>\n                  <!--  <tr> Tag (Table Row) -->\n                  <th>Heading 1</th>\n\n                  <!--- <th> Tag (Table Heading) -->\n                  <th>heading 2</th>\n                </tr>\n                \n                <tr> \n                  <td>Tarun</td>\n                  <!-- <td> Tag (Table Data) -->\n                  <td>BCA</td>\n                </tr>\n              </table>\n\nform :\nThe <form> tag in HTML is used to create a form that collects user input. A form allows\n   users to enter information such as their name, email, password, phone number, address,\n    etc., and submit it to a server for processing. \n\n<form action=\"http://httpbin.org/post\" method=\"post\" onsubmit=\"alert('form Submitted...')\">\n\n      <label for=\"username\">Enter Username</label> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\n\n      <input type=\"text\" id=\"Username\" placeholder=\"Enter Username...\"\n      required name=\"username\">\n\n      <br><br>\n\n      <label for=\"email\">Email</label>\n\n      <input type=\"text\" id=\"Email\" name=\"email\" value=\"tarunpanchal@047gmail.com\" readonly>\n\n      <br><br>\n\n      <label for=\"pass\">Enter Password</label>\n\n      <input type=\"password\" id=\"pass\" placeholder=\"Enter Password\" minlength=\"3\" maxlength=\"8\">\n\n      <br><br>\n\n      <button type=\"submit\">Submit</button>\n\n      <button type=\"reset\">Clear</button>\n\n       <br>\n\n      <label for=\"Country\">Choose Country</label>\n\n\n\n\n\nComplete of Html   ........... Notes ............. Tarun Panchal .....................................\n\n\n\n",
