      "locked": false,
      "text": "                            Semantic Tag ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "                            Semantic Tag ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "I4Os4EqDo22GlX_mUPfiD",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 80.0194165685948,
      "y": 6700.143935571013,
      "width": 902,
      "height": 425,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0Y",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 924259725,
      "version": 686,
      "versionNonce": 896289245,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783315269951,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Semantic tags are HTML elements that clearly describe their meaning to \nthe browser and the developer. Instead of just being generic boxes, these tags use simple, \nplain-english words to explain exactly what types of content goes inside them.\n\n <article>\n <aside>                                          <header>\n <details>                                          \n <figcaption>                                       <nav>\n <figure>\n <header>\n <main>                                 <section>\n <nav>                                                                 <aside>\n <mark>\n <section>                             <article>\n <summary>\n <time>                                                <footer>\n <footer>",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Semantic tags are HTML elements that clearly describe their meaning to \nthe browser and the developer. Instead of just being generic boxes, these tags use simple, \nplain-english words to explain exactly what types of content goes inside them.\n\n <article>\n <aside>                                          <header>\n <details>                                          \n <figcaption>                                       <nav>\n <figure>\n <header>\n <main>                                 <section>\n <nav>                                                                 <aside>\n <mark>\n <section>                             <article>\n <summary>\n <time>                                                <footer>\n <footer>",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "92KTdqkctfvf3BQMS2fyB",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 90.55686350709232,
      "y": 7164.367700973053,
      "width": 820,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0a",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2103552995,
      "version": 584,
      "versionNonce": 612202387,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "1-Csu1CxewlsWAn9utCJc",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1783315246672,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Image Tag            these attributes helps to adjust the size of the image.\n \n\n<img src=\" \" alt=\" \" height=\" \" width=\" \" >\n\nsrc (source) : It contains path of the image (url).\nalt (alternate) : If the image is not able to display properly then, instead of image,\n                    this alternate text will be displayed on the UI.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Image Tag            these attributes helps to adjust the size of the image.\n \n\n<img src=\" \" alt=\" \" height=\" \" width=\" \" >\n\nsrc (source) : It contains path of the image (url).\nalt (alternate) : If the image is not able to display properly then, instead of image,\n                    this alternate text will be displayed on the UI.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
